WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
You're crossing a heath, and
you strike your foot on a stone.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.530
How did it get there?

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.590
It might have lain there forever.

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.890
You walk on.

5
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.930
Then you find a watch lying on the ground.

6
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.460
William Paley said you could
never say the same about that.

7
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.340
If you found a watch on a path,
you'd know someone made it.

8
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.500
Is the world like that watch?

9
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.550
In this mission, you'll open
Paley's watch argument from 1802,

10
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.110
step by step.

11
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.590
Then you'll see how Paley
answered people who doubted him,

12
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.460
and explain his argument
in your own words.

13
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: decide what, if anything, a
watch on a path tells us about the world.
